# SDD Query Language

Spec: QueryLanguage
Purpose:
  Define the query language for the .sdd system. Enables both
  human and AI to query the engineering knowledge graph with
  short, expressive syntax. No SQL or GraphQL required.

Owns: queries/

SyntaxExamples:
  @payment                          — show all knowledge related to payment
  @ddd where used=true              — show DDD references that are active
  show all architecture decisions affecting @payment
  why @task.T2041 uses @skill.idempotency?
  what breaks if @concept.transaction changes?
  find duplicated concepts
  find skills that have no proof
  show unknowns blocking @task.T2041
  show all architecture drift

SimpleSyntax:
  @<concept>                — resolve concept and show related knowledge
  @<type>:<state>           — filter by state (e.g., @task:open, @skill:active)
  @impact:<concept>         — show blast radius of changing a concept
  @unknown:<scope>          — show unknowns (e.g., @unknown:blocking, @unknown:all)
  @risk:<level>             — show tasks at risk level (e.g., @risk:high)
  @domain:<name>            — show all knowledge scoped to a domain

QueryTypes:
  ConceptResolution:
    @payment → architecture + concepts + skills + decisions + tasks + tests

  StateFilter:
    @task:open         — tasks not yet completed
    @skill:active      — skills currently in use
    @decision:approved — approved decisions
    @proof:pending     — proofs awaiting verification

  ImpactAnalysis:
    @impact:@concept.idempotency
    → affected skills, tasks, decisions, docs, tests

  UnknownTracking:
    @unknown:blocking    — unknowns blocking active tasks
    @unknown:unresolved  — all unresolved questions

RiskAware:
  @risk:high    — high-risk tasks/decisions
  @risk:medium  — medium-risk items

DomainScoped:
  @domain:payment     — payment domain knowledge
  @domain:auth        — authentication domain

ReadOrder:
  1  @syntax.sdd
  2  @patterns.sdd

Navigation:
  Syntax: @syntax.sdd
  Patterns: @patterns.sdd

State: +
